oke about the bouquet she threw at her wedding, and he understands exactly what she means: she is ending the marriage. He does not want to fall apart in front of her. His eyebrows relax first; the corners of his mouth start to rise and tremble; he swallows once before his eyes can redden, takes a short breath, and with a half-smile, warm and a little shaky, with clear natural Korean mouth movements fully visible, S1 says: <d>[Korean] 진작 버렸어.</d> He speaks in a clear, warm Korean male voice in the mid to mid-low range, soft and slightly husky from holding back emotion. At 00:05.300, he keeps the half-smile and looks at her steadily, his eyes glossy but no tears falling, until the end.\n\noverall_soundscape: Quiet apartment corridor at night, a faint hum from the ceiling lights, S1's slightly uneven breathing. Only S1's voice is heard; S2 makes no sound.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: N/A"
